  <!-- Section 1: Introduction -->
  <div class="doc-section" id="introduction">
    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>

    <h3>1.1 Purpose of This Document</h3>
    <p>This document provides a comprehensive introduction to Managira and explains how the platform supports the daily operations of schools, school networks, and education administrators. It is designed to help school leaders, teachers, staff, parents, and hub operators understand the platform's core functions, value, and practical use.</p>
    <p>Managira is built to be intuitive and accessible. Users do not need technical expertise to use the platform effectively because it has been designed around the real workflows of educators and school administrators.</p>

    <h3>1.2 About Managira</h3>
    <p>Managira is an all-in-one school management platform that brings together the essential areas of school operations within a single unified system. From enrollment and attendance to assessments, reporting, communication, and school visibility, the platform replaces fragmented tools, spreadsheets, and paper-based processes with a more structured digital environment.</p>
    <p>Managira is designed to reduce administrative workload, strengthen parent communication, improve record accuracy, and support a professional institutional presence through features such as the school website and parent portal. It is suitable for both single schools and larger structures operating under a hub or multi-school model.</p>

    <h3>1.3 Vision and Operating Philosophy</h3>
    <p>Managira was created to give schools technology that works the way schools actually operate. Its design is guided by a practical operating philosophy:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Simplicity first</strong> — Everyday tasks such as marking attendance, generating report cards, and updating school information should be straightforward and efficient.</li>
      <li><strong>Everything in one place</strong> — Student records, academic data, communication, and public-facing content are managed within one system.</li>
      <li><strong>Access for everyone</strong> — Teachers, administrators, parents, and hub operators each see the tools and information appropriate to their role.</li>
      <li><strong>Reliability you can count on</strong> — School operations depend on accurate and dependable systems.</li>
      <li><strong>Built for growth</strong> — Whether a school is expanding enrollment or joining a broader network, Managira scales with that growth.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>1.4 Target Users and Stakeholders</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>School Administrators</strong> — Manage admissions, student records, staff information, school settings, and public-facing content from a central dashboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Teachers and Academic Staff</strong> — Record attendance, enter grades, manage assessments, generate reports, and communicate with parents.</li>
      <li><strong>Finance and Operations Staff</strong> — Manage payment records, deductions, and admissions-related payments.</li>
      <li><strong>Parents and Guardians</strong> — Access grades, attendance records, report cards, and school announcements through a secure portal.</li>
      <li><strong>Hub Operators</strong> — Oversee multiple schools from one central structure while preserving each school's operational identity and branding.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 2: System Overview -->
  <div class="doc-section" id="system-overview">
    <h2>2. System Overview</h2>

    <h3>2.1 What Makes Managira Different</h3>
    <p>Managira is a connected operational system built around the way schools function. Rather than separating attendance, grading, reporting, communication, and administration into disconnected tools, Managira unifies these areas within one platform. Once information is entered, it flows across related workflows — student records entered during enrollment support attendance, assessments, reporting, and parent visibility without repeated data entry.</p>

    <h3>2.2 Core Modules and Capabilities</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Personalized School Website</li>
      <li>Student Management</li>
      <li>Attendance Tracking</li>
      <li>Assessments and Tests</li>
      <li>Report Cards and Transcripts</li>
      <li>Parent Portal</li>
      <li>Online Admissions</li>
      <li>Employee Management</li>
      <li>User Roles and Permissions</li>
      <li>Multi-School Management (Hubs)</li>
      <li>Promotion and Graduation</li>
      <li>Reports and Analytics</li>
      <li>Legal Policies</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.3 User Experience and Role-Based Access</h3>
    <p>When a user logs in, the system presents the tools and information relevant to that user's role. Administrators access school-wide management tools. Teachers access class and student workflows. Parents access only information relevant to their children. Hub Operators access broader visibility across multiple schools.</p>

    <h3>2.4 Multi-School and Hub Management</h3>
    <p>For school groups, networks, or education authorities, Managira supports centralized oversight across multiple schools. Hub users can manage shared visibility, compare school-level performance, and maintain coordination while preserving the identity and operations of each institution.</p>

    <h3>2.5 Deployment and Accessibility</h3>
    <p>Managira is a cloud-based platform accessible through supported web browsers on desktop computers, laptops, tablets, and smartphones. Schools do not need to install software or manage local servers.</p>
  </div>

