    <h3>3.3 Pricing and Payment Options</h3>
    <p>Managira offers flexible billing structures. Schools may select monthly, yearly, or multi-year billing options. Secure payment processing is used for all supported transactions. For hub structures, custom agreements may apply.</p>

    <h3>3.4 Choosing the Right Plan</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Starter Plan</strong> — Core student, attendance, assessment, and reporting tools.</li>
      <li><strong>Professional Plan</strong> — Adds parent access and official transcript capability.</li>
      <li><strong>Premium / Business Plan</strong> — Adds school website, class-based insights, merit sheets, document management, and included multi-school support.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 4: Getting Started -->
  <div class="doc-section" id="getting-started">
    <h2>4. How to Get Started</h2>

    <h3>4.1 Hub Registration</h3>
    <p>If you are setting up a hub or government structure that oversees multiple schools, contact Managira Support through the Help page or by emailing info@managira.com. The team will guide you through setup based on the number of schools involved and features required.</p>

    <h3>4.2 Single School Registration</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to the Managira website and click Sign In.</li>
      <li>Create an account and select Single School as your organization type.</li>
      <li>Choose your plan: Starter, Professional, or Premium.</li>
      <li>Enter your school details including school name, address, proof of organization, and your details as the primary administrator.</li>
      <li>Review the payment summary and confirm the selected plan and billing cycle.</li>
      <li>Complete payment securely. If a free trial is available, billing begins only after the trial period ends.</li>
      <li>Check your email for login details and the onboarding file, then sign in and begin setup.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>4.3 Alternative Setup Option</h3>
    <p>If your organization prefers not to use the online registration process, Managira can prepare a custom contract and complete the setup manually.</p>

    <h3>4.4 Helpful Resources</h3>
    <p>The welcome email includes an onboarding file with setup instructions. Video tutorials are also available to guide users through major workflows. Support remains available through the Help page or by email.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 5: Roles and Permissions -->
  <div class="doc-section" id="roles-permissions">
    <h2>5. Roles and Permissions</h2>

    <h3>5.1 Role Overview</h3>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Role</th><th>Typical Responsibilities</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Manager</td><td>Full operational control including staff management, billing, settings, and all academic workflows.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Supervisor</td><td>Broad academic oversight including admissions, assessments, reports, class management, and transcripts.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Teacher</td><td>Classroom-focused responsibilities including assessments, attendance, and access to assigned class resources.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Main Teacher</td><td>A teacher assigned as lead for a specific class who can manage attendance for that class.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>5.2 What Each Role Can Do</h3>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Permission</th><th>Manager</th><th>Supervisor</th><th>Teacher</th><th>Main Teacher</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Manage staff and role assignments</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Manage students and guardians</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Manage assessments and exams</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Mark attendance</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Manage reports and printing</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Manage records and documents</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Manage promotions</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Approve promotions</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Approve admissions</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Publish announcements and events</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Manage school years and terms</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Manage classes and subjects</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Generate official transcripts</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Manage billing and subscriptions</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Manage organization settings</td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>5.3 File and Document Access</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Managers</strong> can create, edit, delete, and share files with users or classes.</li>
      <li><strong>Supervisors</strong> can do the same only if they have the manage_records permission. Otherwise, they can view only files they created or files shared with them.</li>
      <li><strong>Teachers</strong> cannot create or delete files by default. They can view files only when they created the file, were given direct permission, or the file is shared with a class where they are assigned.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>5.4 Main Teacher and Attendance</h3>
    <p>Managers can access attendance collection for any class. Teachers can collect attendance only for classes where they are assigned as Main Teacher. If a class does not have a Main Teacher assigned, the attendance workflow remains unavailable to teachers until one is assigned.</p>

    <h3>5.5 Best Practices for Using Roles</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Limit Manager accounts to users who genuinely require full control.</li>
      <li>Use Supervisors for academic coordination and day-to-day class and student oversight.</li>
      <li>Keep Teachers focused on instructional workflows.</li>
      <li>Assign Main Teachers each term so responsibility is clear.</li>
      <li>Review file permissions regularly and grant edit access only where necessary.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 6: Setting Up Organization -->
  <div class="doc-section" id="org-setup">
    <h2>6. Setting Up Organization</h2>

    <h3>6.1 Access Requirements</h3>
    <p>Only authenticated users with valid access can complete the setup process.</p>

    <h3>6.2 Welcome Page and Setup Guidance</h3>
    <p>On first login, Managira displays a welcome page with security guidance and setup instructions.</p>

    <h3>6.3 Core Setup Sequence</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Set up school years and terms.</li>
      <li>Create classes using the naming structure that fits the school model.</li>
      <li>Create subjects using the preferred subject structure.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>6.4 Editing Academic Structure</h3>
    <p>If class or subject structures change over time, Managira allows these to be updated without rebuilding the full system configuration.</p>

    <h3>6.5 Graduation Year Configuration</h3>
    <p>Schools can configure graduation school years to assign students to their expected graduation year for progression tracking.</p>

    <h3>6.6 Activate Current Academic Context</h3>
    <p>After setup, the school selects the active school year and active term. This prepares the dashboard and places the system in the correct context.</p>

    <h3>6.7 Enrollment Activation</h3>
    <p>Once classes have been created, enrollment is used to assign students to classes so that class rosters and student participation become active.</p>

    <h3>6.8 Employee Onboarding and Role Assignment</h3>
    <p>Staff can be invited through Employee Management and assigned classes, roles, and relevant operational responsibilities.</p>

    <h3>6.9 School Website Setup</h3>
    <p>Organization setup also includes school website configuration for publishing public information and institutional updates.</p>

    <h3>6.10 Outcome of Setup Completion</h3>
    <p>Once complete, the organization is ready for operational use: active dashboards, student and class operations, teacher participation, and public communication through the school website.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 7: School Website -->
  <div class="doc-section" id="school-website">
    <h2>7. School Website</h2>

    <h3>7.1 Purpose and Strategic Value</h3>
    <p>The Managira School Website gives each school a professional public presence where parents, guardians, prospective families, and the wider community can access current and reliable information about the institution.</p>

    <h3>7.2 What Schools Can Publish</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Hero images and banners</li>
      <li>Image galleries</li>
      <li>About sections</li>
      <li>Announcements and updates</li>
      <li>Event information</li>
      <li>Contact and profile details</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>7.3 Self-Service Editing</h3>
    <p>Authorized users can manage website content directly: upload and replace images, create/update/reorder/remove sections, edit About information, adjust layout and style options, and publish updates to the live website.</p>

    <h3>7.4 School Website and Admissions</h3>
    <p>When online admissions are enabled, the school website also acts as a public entry point for applications, connecting public engagement with admissions intake.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 8: Admissions -->
  <div class="doc-section" id="admissions">
    <h2>8. Admissions</h2>

    <h3>8.1 Admissions Model Overview</h3>
    <p>Managira supports two admissions pathways:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Self Admission</strong> — Parents or guardians apply through the school website.</li>
      <li><strong>School Managed Admission</strong> — Authorized users admit students through internal workflows.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>8.2 Self Admission Through the School Website</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>The school enables public admissions on its website.</li>
      <li>The parent or guardian opens the admissions page.</li>
      <li>The applicant enters student and guardian details.</li>
      <li>Any required admissions payment is initiated according to school settings.</li>
      <li>The application is submitted and stored as pending for school review.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>8.3 School Managed Admission</h3>
    <p>Schools can admit students through manual entry, bulk-assisted workflows, and image/document-based extraction workflows.</p>

    <h3>8.4 Data Captured During Admission</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Student identity and demographic details</li>
      <li>Class assignment</li>
      <li>Subject association</li>
      <li>School year and term context</li>
      <li>Expected graduation or year group placement</li>
      <li>Guardian information</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>8.5 Admissions Queue and Decision Process</h3>
    <p>Pending admissions are reviewed by authorized school users before approval. The process includes visibility of pending applications, review and editing, approval or rejection, and communication of the decision.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 9: Attendance Tracking -->
  <div class="doc-section" id="attendance">
    <h2>9. Attendance Tracking</h2>

    <h3>9.1 What It Does</h3>
    <p>Attendance tracking in Managira is designed to be fast, accurate, and practical for everyday school use.</p>

    <h3>9.2 How It Works</h3>
    <p>Teachers record attendance for assigned classes. The system captures each student's attendance status and stores a full attendance history. Built-in efficiencies help reduce repetitive work when attendance patterns are routine.</p>

    <h3>9.3 Visibility and Alerts</h3>
    <p>School leaders can review attendance summaries by class, grade, or across the school. Parents can view attendance records through the parent portal where enabled.</p>

    <h3>9.4 Alignment with the School Calendar</h3>
    <p>Attendance settings can be aligned with the school calendar so that holidays, exam periods, and special events are handled appropriately.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 10: Assessments and Tests -->
  <div class="doc-section" id="assessments">
    <h2>10. Assessments and Tests</h2>

    <h3>10.1 What It Does</h3>
    <p>Managira allows schools to build assessment structures that match their own academic model, whether they use letter grades, percentages, or a custom scoring system.</p>

    <h3>10.2 How It Works</h3>
    <p>Authorized users create assessment structures for each class and subject. Schools decide how many tests, exams, assignments, or other components contribute to the final grade and assign a weight to each one.</p>

    <h3>10.3 Controlled Access</h3>
    <p>Assessment periods can be opened and closed according to the school calendar. Only authorized users can enter or edit scores during active periods.</p>

    <h3>10.4 Visibility for Parents and Reporting</h3>
    <p>Assessment results flow into report cards and the parent portal, helping parents see more than just final grades.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 11: Reports -->
  <div class="doc-section" id="reports">
    <h2>11. Reports</h2>

    <h3>11.1 What It Does</h3>
    <p>Managira transforms academic and operational data into professional reports, from student report cards to broader school-level reporting.</p>

    <h3>11.2 Student Report Cards</h3>
    <p>Schools can generate terminal report cards using recorded grades, attendance, and teacher comments. Reports can be printed or shared digitally.</p>

    <h3>11.3 School Level Reports</h3>
    <p>School leaders can access reporting on enrollment, attendance, grade distribution, and related academic indicators.</p>

    <h3>11.4 Parent Communication</h3>
    <p>Reports can be shared with parents through the parent portal or by email, depending on the school's configuration.</p>

    <h3>11.5 Security</h3>
    <p>All reports respect user roles and permissions. Sensitive information is visible only to authorized users and the student's own parents or guardians.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 12: Promotion and Graduation -->
  <div class="doc-section" id="promotion">
    <h2>12. Promotion and Graduation</h2>

    <h3>12.1 What It Does</h3>
    <p>Promotion and graduation workflows help schools manage student progression in a structured way.</p>

    <h3>12.2 Promotion Decisions</h3>
    <p>At the end of a term or academic year, schools can review student performance and apply promotion rules based on school policy.</p>

    <h3>12.3 Flexible Rules</h3>
    <p>Schools control their own promotion criteria, including score thresholds, attendance expectations, and other internal rules.</p>

    <h3>12.4 Execution Options</h3>
    <p>Promotions can be applied immediately or scheduled after term closure. Authorized users can review, reverse, or correct actions where needed.</p>

    <h3>12.5 Graduation and Archiving</h3>
    <p>When students graduate or leave, records can be archived while preserving the full academic history for future reference.</p>
  </div>

